## Recommended Paper

For the best results, use:

- 15 × 15 cm or 20 × 20 cm square paper
- Thin origami or kami paper
- Paper that holds creases well but is still easy to inflate
- Yellow paper for a classic baby chick appearance
- Single-color paper to emphasize the silhouette and folds

Larger paper is recommended for the first attempt because the folds around the head, beak, and feet are easier to shape.

## Folding Tips

- Make the initial folds as accurately as possible to keep the model symmetrical.
- Press the pre-creases firmly before performing the sink fold.
- Keep both sides aligned when shaping the body.
- Fold the beak approximately as shown in the diagram; no exact reference point is required.
- Make the mountain folds on both sides evenly to create a balanced head shape.
- Blow gently into the opening at the end to inflate the body without deforming the folds.
- After inflating, gently adjust the body, wings, feet, and beak with your fingers.

## About This Diagram

This diagram presents the complete folding sequence for the **Baby Chick Origami** in 20 illustrated steps.

The model is folded from a single square sheet of paper and is inflated near the end to create its three-dimensional body.

Standard origami symbols, arrows, mountain folds, and a sink fold are used throughout the diagram to make each folding movement easier to understand.

The printable PDF provides a convenient step-by-step reference that can be followed without pausing or rewinding a video.

